-- title:
--   Local type of a normalised connecting finite idele
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ be nonzero, let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order, i.e. it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, is finitely generated, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, and equals every order containing it; let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $m$ a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$. Assume $m$ lies in [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$, the additive subgroup generated by the $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele; assume $N\cdot m^{-1}$ lies in the same subgroup; and assume the relative index of $\Lambda_1\cap\,$[`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31)$\,\Lambda_1\,m$ (the elements of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose image in the adelic algebra lies in $m\,\widehat{\Lambda_1}\,m^{-1}$) inside $\Lambda_1$ is exactly $N$. Then: (i) for every finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ with $N\notin v$, the image of $m$ at $v$ lies in [`Submodule.localBoxUnits`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45) $\Lambda_1\,v$, i.e. both it and its inverse lie in the additive subgroup generated by $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$, $c$ a $v$-adic integer; and (ii) for every $v$ and every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\in v$ and $\ell\mid N$, the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is not a division ring, and there is a ring isomorphism $\varphi$ of it with $M_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ sending $1\otimes r$ to $r\cdot 1$, under which the local box of $\Lambda_1$ at $v$ is the set of elements with all entries $v$-integral, together with $k_1,k_2\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ whose entries and whose inverses' entries are $v$-integral and with $\varphi(m_v)=k_1\,\mathrm{diag}(1,\ell^{\,v_\ell(N)})\,k_2$.
--
--   This is the local elementary-divisor analysis of a connecting idele whose associated intersection of orders has index $N$: away from $N$ the idele is locally a unit of the order, and at each prime dividing $N$ the algebra is split and the idele has elementary divisors $(1,\ell^{v_\ell(N)})$ with respect to a local maximal order. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld tower, in the verification that the intersected orders are Eichler of the expected level and in the description of the Hecke double cosets at a given level.
